  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTION &amp; MONITORING OF CERULEAN &amp; GOLDEN-WINGED WARBLERS IN COLUMBIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Colombia has the richest bird diversity in the world with 193 Neotropical migrants from North America. Owing to its strategic geographical position, almost all flyway corridors from North and Central America to South America pass through Colombia. Forty-seven Neotropical migrant species of conservation concern are found in Colombia. Importantly, Colombia holds globally significant wintering populations of two of these species: the Cerulean Warbler and Golden-winged Warbler. This project will benefit cerulean and golden-winged warbler habitat in Colombia by acquiring over 9,000 acres, conducting management, monitoring and restoration activities in tropical forests, as well as restoring forested acres and training staff.</narrative>
  </description>
